<p>Omnexa (the “Platform”) is operated by Meta Realty Sdn Bhd, a company registered in Malaysia under registration number 202201040486 (1486183-V) (“we”, “us”, or “our”). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, store, protect, and otherwise process personal data in connection with Omnexa.</p>
<p>This Policy applies when you register for or use an Omnexa account, use a company workspace, connect messaging or third-party services, upload knowledge or business data, communicate through the Platform, make a purchase, contact support, or otherwise interact with Omnexa.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s1">1. What Omnexa Does</h2>
<p>Omnexa is an AI chatbot management workspace that includes account and company workspace management, chatbot configuration, Knowledge Base and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), PDF and website knowledge, messaging and conversation management, CRM and lead management, broadcasts and campaigns, analytics, team management, AI model and provider configuration, subscriptions, AI Credits, billing, support operations, and related administration features.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s2">2. Personal Data We May Collect</h2>
<h3 class="sub">Account, Identity, and Workspace Data</h3>
<ul>
<li>name, email address, and other contact information;</li>
<li>company, business, school, organisation, or workspace information;</li>
<li>user role, workspace membership, invitations, account status, and profile information;</li>
<li>registration information, login activity, and account preferences;</li>
<li>information received through Google Sign-In where you choose to use it, such as your Google account identity and verified email information.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="sub">Customer, Lead, CRM, and Contact Data</h3>
<p>When a Customer uses Omnexa to manage customer conversations, CRM records, leads, or contacts, the Platform may process:</p>
<ul>
<li>names, telephone numbers, email addresses, and messaging/contact identifiers;</li>
<li>lead records, status, assignment, notes, and related CRM information;</li>
<li>customer enquiries, customer-provided details, and conversation history;</li>
<li>other information entered by the Customer or provided by the Customer’s contacts through connected channels.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="sub">Messages, Conversations, and Media</h3>
<ul>
<li>incoming and outgoing messages;</li>
<li>chatbot and human-agent conversations;</li>
<li>sender and recipient identifiers;</li>
<li>message timestamps, delivery or channel information, and conversation metadata;</li>
<li>attachments, files, images, media, or other content exchanged through supported messaging features.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="sub">Knowledge, Website, and AI Data</h3>
<ul>
<li>documents, PDF files, website content, FAQs, product information, service information, and other knowledge sources;</li>
<li>chatbot instructions, prompts, behaviour settings, configuration, and training content;</li>
<li>knowledge chunks or retrieved context used to support RAG-based responses;</li>
<li>AI-generated replies, summaries, classifications, suggestions, reports, or other AI-assisted output.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="sub">Billing, Subscription, and AI Credit Data</h3>
<ul>
<li>subscription plan, billing period, feature entitlement, and account billing status;</li>
<li>subscription and top-up order information;</li>
<li>payment status, transaction reference, amount, and confirmation information received from payment providers;</li>
<li>AI Credit purchases, balances, allocations, consumption, and usage information.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where a third-party payment provider processes the transaction, we generally do not receive or store complete payment-card, online-banking, or other sensitive payment credentials handled directly by that provider.</p>
<h3 class="sub">Technical, Security, and Operational Data</h3>
<ul>
<li>IP address, browser information, device information, and request metadata;</li>
<li>login activity, usage activity, feature usage, and operational events;</li>
<li>security events, error information, diagnostic information, and application or provider-related logs;</li>
<li>information reasonably necessary to investigate failures, prevent abuse, maintain service reliability, or protect the Platform.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="sub">Support and Administrative Data</h3>
<ul>
<li>Help Desk or support requests, replies, attachments, and account information used to investigate a case;</li>
<li>support-case status, priority, assignment, and activity history;</li>
<li>platform administration and audit information, including administrative actions, affected resources, metadata, and timestamps where applicable.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s3">3. How We Collect Personal Data</h2>
<p>We may collect personal data from the following sources:</p>
<ul>
<li>directly from you when you register, configure an account, submit information, make a purchase, or contact support;</li>
<li>from your company or workspace administrator when they invite, add, or manage you;</li>
<li>from Google Sign-In when you choose to authenticate using Google;</li>
<li>from Customer-uploaded documents, PDFs, websites, knowledge sources, CRM records, or other content;</li>
<li>from WhatsApp, Telegram, WaSender, and other connected messaging or communication services;</li>
<li>from customers, leads, contacts, or other end users who communicate with a Customer through Omnexa;</li>
<li>from payment providers in connection with payment status, transaction confirmation, or billing events;</li>
<li>automatically through normal use of the Platform, including technical, security, and operational logs.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s4">4. Why We Use Personal Data</h2>
<p>We may process personal data for purposes including:</p>
<ul>
<li>creating, verifying, authenticating, and managing accounts and company workspaces;</li>
<li>supporting Google Sign-In, invitation-based onboarding, team membership, roles, and access controls;</li>
<li>creating, configuring, operating, and managing AI chatbots;</li>
<li>processing and routing customer conversations and messages;</li>
<li>providing inbox, conversation, CRM, lead-management, broadcast, and campaign functionality;</li>
<li>providing Knowledge Base, PDF, website, and RAG functionality;</li>
<li>generating AI-assisted replies, summaries, classifications, recommendations, reports, or other AI-enabled features;</li>
<li>operating subscription plans, feature access, billing, payment status, AI Credits, and usage limits;</li>
<li>providing analytics, usage information, service monitoring, and administrative views;</li>
<li>providing Help Desk, support-case, and customer support functions;</li>
<li>detecting, preventing, and investigating fraud, misuse, unauthorised access, security incidents, or service failures;</li>
<li>maintaining, troubleshooting, securing, and improving the Platform;</li>
<li>sending service-related, support, security, billing, subscription, and account communications;</li>
<li>complying with applicable legal, regulatory, contractual, and record-keeping obligations.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s5">5. Required and Optional Information</h2>
<p>Certain personal data is required to create or maintain an account, verify identity, operate a workspace, process a payment, connect a service, or provide a requested feature. Required fields or information will generally be identified by the relevant registration, configuration, billing, or service flow.</p>
<p>If required information is not provided, we may be unable to create or verify an account, provide the relevant feature, complete a transaction, maintain access, or respond to a request. Information that is not required for the relevant purpose may be optional.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s6">6. Customer Data and End-User Data</h2>
<p>Omnexa is a business platform. Customers may use it to process personal data relating to their own customers, leads, contacts, employees, or other individuals. Depending on the circumstances, the Customer may act as the data controller for that information and Omnexa may process such data on the Customer’s behalf as a service provider or data processor.</p>
<p>Customers are responsible for ensuring that they have the necessary authority, privacy notices, permissions, consent, or other lawful basis required to collect, upload, message, broadcast to, or otherwise process personal data through Omnexa.</p>
<p>Customers must not use Omnexa to collect or process personal data in a manner that violates applicable law, third-party platform rules, or the rights of individuals.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s7">7. AI Processing</h2>
<p>Omnexa supports configurable AI providers and models. Information submitted to AI-enabled features may be used to generate replies, summaries, classifications, recommendations, reports, knowledge retrieval results, or other AI-assisted output.</p>
<p>Depending on the feature and configuration, relevant prompts, conversation context, knowledge content, or retrieved information may be transmitted to third-party AI service providers. Current system integrations may include services such as Cloudflare, OpenRouter and DeepSeek for applicable AI functionality.</p>
<p>Customers should avoid submitting unnecessary sensitive, confidential, or unrelated personal data into AI prompts, chatbot instructions, documents, websites, or knowledge sources. Customers remain responsible for deciding what information is submitted and for reviewing AI-generated output before use.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s8">8. Messaging and Third-Party Integrations</h2>
<p>Omnexa may integrate with or rely on third-party services, including Meta/WhatsApp, Telegram, WaSender, Google Sign-In, AI service providers, payment gateways, database and infrastructure providers, monitoring services, and other external platforms required to provide the Services.</p>
<p>When you connect or use a third-party service, information may be transmitted between Omnexa and that provider as reasonably necessary to operate the integration. For messaging services, this may include contact identifiers, messages, attachments, delivery information, and conversation metadata.</p>
<p>Third-party services may process information under their own terms and privacy policies. Their availability, retention practices, and data-handling requirements may differ from ours.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s9">9. Service Providers and Disclosure of Personal Data</h2>
<p>We may disclose personal data where reasonably necessary to:</p>
<ul>
<li>operate Omnexa and provide connected messaging, AI, authentication, database, hosting, payment, monitoring, and support functions;</li>
<li>process transactions, subscriptions, or AI Credit purchases;</li>
<li>deliver messages or content through Customer-selected communication channels;</li>
<li>provide technical support, investigate incidents, and maintain service reliability;</li>
<li>protect Omnexa, our Customers, users, and third parties from fraud, abuse, security threats, or unlawful activity;</li>
<li>comply with applicable law, legal process, court orders, or lawful requests from authorities;</li>
<li>support a merger, acquisition, restructuring, financing, or sale of all or part of the business, subject to applicable legal requirements.</li>
</ul>
<p>Examples of current technology services used by the system may include Supabase for backend/database services, Cloudflare for AI processing, document storage and message queuing, OpenRouter and DeepSeek for applicable AI services, Sentry for error monitoring, Google for Sign-In, and supported messaging or payment providers. Providers may change as the Platform develops.</p>
<p>We do not sell personal data to advertisers.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s10">10. Payment Information</h2>
<p>Payment transactions may be processed by third-party payment gateways. Those providers may collect information directly from you that is necessary to complete a transaction.</p>
<p>Omnexa may receive and store transaction-related information such as the order reference, amount, payment status, gateway transaction reference, payment method category, and confirmation or reconciliation information. The payment provider’s own privacy terms may apply to information it processes directly.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s11">11. International Data Transfers</h2>
<p>Some service providers used by Omnexa may operate infrastructure, provide support, or process information outside Malaysia. As a result, personal data may be transferred to or processed in other countries.</p>
<p>Where cross-border transfers occur, we will take reasonable steps to comply with applicable Malaysian personal-data protection requirements and to apply appropriate safeguards where required.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s12">12. Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal data against unauthorised access, disclosure, misuse, alteration, loss, or destruction.</p>
<p>Depending on the feature, these measures may include password hashing, token-based authentication, account and role controls, company/workspace separation, protected administrative access, secure handling of supported files, monitoring, and other safeguards appropriate to the Platform.</p>
<p>No online service, communication channel, or method of electronic storage can guarantee absolute security. Customers are also responsible for protecting account credentials, managing workspace access, and maintaining the security of connected third-party accounts.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s13">13. Cookies, Browser Storage, and Similar Technologies</h2>
<p>Omnexa does not currently rely on cookies as the primary mechanism for user authentication. The Platform uses token-based authentication and may use browser storage or similar technologies to maintain an authenticated session, application state, preferences, or security-related functionality.</p>
<p>Third-party services used in connection with Omnexa, such as Google Sign-In or external websites, may use their own cookies or similar technologies on their own domains. If Omnexa later introduces non-essential cookies or tracking technologies that require consent, we will provide an appropriate notice or consent mechanism where required.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s14">14. Data Retention</h2>
<p>We retain personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, including to provide the Services, maintain accounts and subscriptions, support business and security records, resolve disputes, investigate abuse, meet accounting or legal obligations, and maintain appropriate audit information.</p>
<p>Different categories of information may be retained for different periods. When personal data is no longer reasonably required, we may delete, anonymise, or otherwise dispose of it in accordance with our applicable retention practices, backup processes, and legal requirements.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s15">15. Data Accuracy</h2>
<p>You should provide accurate, complete, and current personal data and update account information when it changes. Customers are responsible for maintaining the accuracy of CRM, lead, contact, knowledge, and other data they enter or upload.</p>
<p>We may take reasonable steps to maintain the accuracy of personal data where appropriate for the purposes for which it is processed.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s16">16. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
<p>Subject to applicable law and relevant exceptions, you may have rights in relation to personal data we hold about you, including the right to:</p>
<ul>
<li>request access to personal data held about you;</li>
<li>request correction of inaccurate, incomplete, misleading, or outdated personal data;</li>
<li>withdraw consent where processing depends on consent, subject to applicable legal and service consequences;</li>
<li>ask questions or make requests regarding how your personal data is processed;</li>
<li>exercise any other rights available under applicable Malaysian data-protection law.</li>
</ul>
<p>We may need to verify your identity before completing certain requests. If your data is controlled by one of our Customers, we may direct you to that Customer or assist the Customer in responding, depending on the circumstances.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s17">17. Marketing and Service Communications</h2>
<p>Where permitted and based on the appropriate preference or permission, we may send optional product updates, offers, promotions, or related marketing communications. You may opt out of optional marketing communications using the unsubscribe method provided or by contacting us.</p>
<p>Service-related communications, including security alerts, billing notices, subscription updates, account notices, support replies, and important operational messages, are not treated as optional marketing communications.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s18">18. Children and Minors</h2>
<p>Omnexa is primarily intended for business users. A person registering and managing a business account should be at least 18 years old or otherwise have the legal capacity to enter into an agreement.</p>
<p>If a Customer uses Omnexa to communicate with or process personal data relating to children or minors, including in an education-related context, the Customer is responsible for ensuring that it has the appropriate authority, notices, consent, and safeguards required by applicable law.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s19">19. Personal Data Breaches</h2>
<p>If a personal data breach occurs, we will take reasonable steps to contain, investigate, and address the incident. Where required by applicable law, we will make notifications to the relevant regulator and/or affected individuals in accordance with applicable requirements.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s20">20. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to Omnexa, our service providers, legal requirements, or our data-handling practices. The updated version will state its effective or “Last Updated” date. Where a change is material, we may provide reasonable notice through email, the Platform, an in-app notification, or another appropriate method.</p>
<h2 class="sec" id="en-s21">21. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If you have questions, requests, complaints, or concerns about this Privacy Policy or the way Omnexa handles personal data, you may contact us at:</p>
